      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 46,
      "text": "4. Learned counsel for petitioners requested that a similar order be passed as in C.C.No.451 of 2025,\nwherein the learned Single Judge of this Court, while closing the contempt case, granted liberty to the petitioners therein to file an Execution Petition before the competent civil Court.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 5144,
      "end": 5433,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "C.C.No.451 of 2025",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 5226,
          "end": 5244
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 47,
      "text": "5. The Hon'ble Apex Court in R.N.Dey and others v. Bhagyabati Pramanik and others 1 held that proper forum to execute the award is competent civil Court.",
